> **Before any UI work, read [`docs/design-language.md`](./docs/design-language.md)** —
> the full house language (bands, signal, type, motion, glyphs, contrast gate,
> banned list, and a self-check). It is deliberately not summarised here: this
> file loads every session, that one loads only when you touch UI.

The app follows the house **CodaSignal "Signal"** design language: full-bleed
bands that alternate dark (`#0e0f0d`) and light (`#f2f2ee`), one chromatic signal
in four temperatures (Jade is the default) that only ever marks the second line
of a heading, live data, or a list number, fixed status colours that never theme
(degraded `#c99a3a`, incident `#c9553a`, idle = faint ink), Archivo at 600/500
with tight negative tracking for everything readable, and JetBrains Mono for
every label/tag/data/glyph/code line. Depth is a hairline; a panel adds one soft
shadow on a light band and none on a dark one. No serif, no italic, no second
hue, no gradients, no icon library.

**Hard rules:** no hardcoded hex or magic numbers in components — tokens only
(`colors` · `spacing`/`radii`/`borderWidth`/`layout` · `typography` · `duration` ·
`icons`/`glyphs`). The signal never fills a button. Focus is always visible: a
1pt `colors.accent` border plus a `layout.focusRing` (3pt) `colors.focusRing`
wash. Numbers are tabular (`fontVariant`). Press feedback is a colour move or a
1pt nudge, never a shadow. Motion renders in its final state when
`AccessibilityInfo.isReduceMotionEnabled()` is true.

